"""Central stages 64–93: source text, glosses and comparison forms stay separate."""
from zhongshan_next30 import R

ROWS = [
R('r06-baishi','白石','Mount Baishi','白石阳惠水南注洛、多水玉；阴涧水西北注榖、多麋石櫨丹，郭注皆未闻不强定矿物。两源侧、流向分存。','Forty li west is Mount Baishi. Hui water rises on its sunny side and flows south into the Luo, with water jade. Jian water rises on its shaded side and flows northwest into Gu water, with mi stone and ludan.','Guo Pu leaves the latter products unknown. The two source sides and directions remain separate.'),
R('r06-gu','榖山','Mount Gu','西五十里为榖，上榖下桑。爽水西北注榖水、多碧绿，郭注紵麻涧为古名说，不作现代河道定位。','Fifty li west is Mount Gu, with gu trees above and mulberry below. Shuang water flows northwest into Gu water and has bi-green material.','The Zhuma-jian name is commentary, not a measured modern river identification.'),
R('r06-mi','密山','Mount Mi','西七十二里为密，阳玉阴铁，豪水南注洛多旋龟，鸟首鼈尾、判木声。郭注疑非荥阳密山，不认定现代同址；鼈尾不借南山虺尾。189在22页。','Seventy-two li west is Mount Mi, with jade on its sunny side and iron on its shaded side. Hao water flows south into the Luo and has Xuangui with bird heads, softshell-turtle tails and a splitting-wood sound. There is no vegetation.','Guo Pu doubts a contemporary namesake identification. Unit 189 is on scan 22. This tail is not the Southern account’s snake tail; ordinary turtle limbs and shell styling are artistic.'),
R('r06-changshi','長石','Mount Changshi','西百里为长石，无草木、多金玉；西共谷多竹，共水西南注洛多鸣石。似玉色青、远闻及石鼓长注跨192—193，仅作郭注例述，不补现代声学定论。','A hundred li west is Mount Changshi, without vegetation and with gold and jade. Gong valley to its west has bamboo; Gong water flows southwest into the Luo and has ringing stones.','The long ringing-stone commentary spans 192–193. Its cited colors, sounds and drum-shaped example do not establish modern mineral or acoustic identity.'),
R('r06-mountain-194','𫝊山','Mountain of unit 194','西百四十里为录字𫝊山，无草木、多瑶碧；厌染水南注洛多人鱼，西林名墦冢，穀水东注洛多珚玉。山名录字不强定近形字或读音，缺字图冢仅阅读层恢复。','A hundred and forty li west is the mountain named in unit 194, without vegetation and with yaobi. Yanran water flows south into the Luo and has renyu. A western forest is named Fanzhong; Gu water flows east into the Luo and has yan jade.','The captured mountain-name glyph is retained without forcing a pronunciation. The forest name’s missing zhong marker is restored only in the reading layer. The source-side Gu account stays distinct from the recipient index.'),
R('r06-tuo','橐山','Mount Tuo','西五十里橐山多樗𣖾木，阳金玉阴铁萧；𣖾木长注跨198—200分存。橐水北注河、脩辟鱼黽状白喙，郭注黽蛙属，鸱声不添翅。198在23页。','Fifty li west is Mount Tuo, with chu and bei trees, gold and jade on its sunny side, and iron and xiao on its shaded side. Tuo water flows north into the He and has Xiubi, frog-like with white mouths and kite-like cries.','The long tree gloss spans 198–200. The kite comparison is sound only; frog limbs, other colors and posture are artistic. Unit 198 is on scan 23.'),
R('r06-changzheng','常烝','Mount Changzheng','西九十里常烝无草木多垩，潐水东北注河多苍玉，菑水北注河。两水不并，音谯只释潐水名。','Ninety li west is Mount Changzheng, without vegetation and with e. Jiao water flows northeast into the He and has cang jade; Zai water flows north into the He.','The two water accounts and the Jiao pronunciation gloss remain separate.'),
R('r06-kuafu','夸父','Mount Kuafu','西九十里夸父多㯶柟竹箭、㸲牛羬羊鷩，均仅列名不借异篇形貌；北桃林广圆三百里、多马，郭注野马山羊山牛为外层例述。湖水北注河多珚玉，不因山名补逐日巨人。','Ninety li west is Mount Kuafu, with zong, nan and arrow bamboo, zuo cattle, qianyang and Bi birds. A northern forest named Taolin spans a stated three hundred li and has horses. Hu water flows north into the He and has yan jade.','The mountain name does not add a giant chasing the sun. The listed animals receive no borrowed anatomy; the wild-horse and other animal gloss continues across 207–208.'),
R('r06-yanghua','陽華','Mount Yanghua','西九十里阳华，阳金玉阴青雄黄；苦辛树状如橚、实如瓜，古食效分录。杨水西南注洛多人鱼；门水东北注河多玄䃤，𦁎姑水出阴东注门；门水出河七百九十里入雒的另述照录不强改。','Ninety li west is Mount Yanghua, with gold and jade on its sunny side, green xionghuang on its shaded side, shuyu and kuxin plants. Yang water flows southwest into the Luo; Men water flows northeast into the He, while Jigu water rises on the shaded side and flows east into Men water. Copper is abundant above.','The separate seven-hundred-and-ninety-li Men-water statement is retained even where its relationship to the earlier direction is unclear. Ancient eating claims and the black-stone gloss do not establish modern uses.'),
R('r06-summary','次六总括','Sixth-range summary and rites','縞羝首平逢至阳华，十四山七百九十里，岳在其中、六月如诸岳祠法。安宁为古祭述，不编未名神形；216实际在25页末。','The sixth range from Pingfeng to Yanghua reports fourteen mountains and 790 li, with a sacred peak among them, sacrificed to in the sixth month according to the peak rites, with a claim of peace.','No additional anatomy or named deity is supplied. Unit 216 is at the end of scan 25; the sixth month is glossed as the middle of the year.'),
R('r07-xiuyu','休與','Mount Xiuyu','中次七苦山首休与，帝台棋五色有文如鹑卵，是祷百神之石，不当鹌鹑实生。帝台与百神无独立形貌留占位；风条蓍状赤叶丛本、可为箭笴，古用途照录。','The seventh range begins at Mount Xiuyu. Ditai’s qi stones have five colors and markings and resemble quail eggs; they are used in prayers to many gods. Fengtiao resembles shi, with red leaves and clustered bases, and is said to make arrow shafts.','Eggs compare the stone shape, not native birds. Ditai and the many gods have no independent anatomy here; the eating and ritual claims remain ancient.'),
R('r07-guzhong','皷鍾','Mount Guzhong','东三百里皷钟，帝台觞百神地。焉酸方茎黄花圆叶三成，郭注叶三重不补三茎；上砺下砥。225在26页，举觞注跨224—225，不移作草形。','Three hundred li east is Mount Guzhong, where Ditai gives drink to many gods. Yansuan has square stems, yellow flowers and round leaves in three layers; li stone is above and di stone below.','The banquet gloss spans 224–225 and is separate from the plant. Three layers refer to leaves, not three stems; the ancient poison wording is not an instruction.'),
R('r07-guyao','姑媱','Mount Guyao','东二百里姑媱，帝女女尸死而化䔄草；女尸不据称号补人像或尸体。草叶胥成黄花、实如菟丘，郭注菟丝为比拟，不与太室白花黑实同名䔄草合并。','Two hundred li east is Mount Guyao, where the emperor’s daughter Nüshi dies and becomes yaocao, with layered leaves, yellow flowers and fruit compared with tuqiu.','The daughter has no independent anatomy here and is not shown as a corpse. Commentary compares tuqiu with tusi; this plant stays separate from the Taishi namesake.'),
R('r07-ku','苦山','Mount Ku','东二十里苦山，山膏如逐、郭注豚字，赤若丹火善詈；火为色比不画火。黄棘黄花圆叶实如兰，无条圆叶无茎赤花不实，古食效与生育字义分存。','Twenty li east is Mount Ku. Shangao is pig-like, cinnabar-red and good at cursing. Huangji has yellow flowers, round leaves and lan-like fruit. Wutiao has round leaves, no stem, red flowers and no fruit.','Pig form follows the text and gloss; cursing supplies no human mouth and cinnabar fire no literal flame. The plant claims are ancient. Unit 234 is on scan 27.'),
R('r07-du','堵山','Mount Du','东二十七里堵山，天愚居之多怪风雨，无神形不画雷神。天楄方茎葵状，服不㖶为古食述，音鞭与不噎义分别录。','Twenty-seven li east is Mount Du, dwelling of Tianyu, with unusual winds and rain. Tianbian has square stems and a mallow-like form, with an ancient eating claim.','Tianyu has no independent anatomy and is not turned into a thunder god. Pronunciation and the choking gloss belong to the plant account.'),
R('r07-fanggao','放皐','Mount Fanggao','东五十二里放皐，明水南注伊、多苍玉，山名有効牧异字。蒙木槐叶黄花不实；文文蜂状枝尾反舌善呼，分叉数、蜂足翼与配色为解释，不把叫声补成人面。','Fifty-two li east is Mount Fanggao. Ming water flows south into the Yi and has cang jade. Meng trees have huai-like leaves, yellow flowers and no fruit. Wenwen is bee-like with a branched tail and reversed tongue and is good at calling.','The exact branch count, ordinary insect legs and wings, colors and pose are artistic. Calling supplies no human face; the mountain-name variants remain separate.'),
R('r07-da-241','大𩇵','Da mountain (unit 241)','东五十七里大𩇵，山名录字不强定音、不并后文大騩。多㻬琈玉麋玉，牛伤榆叶方茎苍伤、根苍文，刺义为郭注。狂水出阳西南注伊，多三足龟；郭注外地三足六眼引例独立列参照，不把六眼填给本山龟。','Fifty-seven li east is Da mountain of unit 241, with tufu and mi jade and Niushang plants. Kuang water rises on its sunny side and flows southwest into the Yi and has three-legged turtles.','Three legs are explicit locally. The six-eyed turtle is an outside-locality commentary example, given a separate comparison card rather than added to the native turtle. Unit 243 is on scan 28.'),
R('r07-banshi','半石','Mount Banshi','东七十里半石，嘉荣生而秀、赤叶赤花不实，初穗后叶花生穗间据郭注。来需水出阳西注伊，鯩鱼鲋状黑文；合水出阴北注洛，鰧鱼鳜状苍文赤尾，居逵为水中通道不补足。252在29页。','Seventy li east is Mount Banshi. Jiarong sprouts into ears and has red leaves and flowers but no fruit. Laixu water rises on the sunny side and flows west into the Yi, with Lun fish resembling fu and bearing black markings. He water rises on the shaded side and flows north into the Luo, with Teng fish, gui-like with blue-green markings and red tails.','Guo Pu describes the growth sequence and, separately, gui fish with large mouths and eyes and fine scales. Channel dwelling supplies no legs; the medical claims are ancient.'),
R('r07-shaoshi','少室','Mount Shaoshi','东五十里少室，百草木成囷未详；帝休杨叶枝五衢黄花黑实，五衢为枝交错五出不擅作五主干。休水北注洛，䱱鱼比拟𥂕蜼及足白而对郭注未详，留占位不借猴尾鱼形。','Fifty li east is Mount Shaoshi. Dixiu has yang-like leaves, five-way branches, yellow flowers and black fruit. Xiu water flows north into the Luo and has Ti fish, compared with an uncertain form, with long spurs and paired white feet.','The unknown comparison and uncertain paired-foot wording retain a placeholder. Five-way branching does not specify five trunks. Guo Pu’s white-jade-paste and immortality statement is a separate ancient commentary claim.'),
R('r07-taishi','泰室','Mount Taishi','东三十里泰室，栯木蔾叶赤理；䔄草术状白花黑实泽如蘡薁，与姑媱黄花草分开。美石次玉、启母化石生启为郭注，不据故事补神像。261在30页。','Thirty li east is Mount Taishi. You trees have li-like leaves with red grain. Yaocao resembles zhu, with white flowers and glossy black fruit compared with yingyu; fine stones are abundant above.','This plant is distinct from Guyao’s yellow-flowered yaocao. Qimu’s transformation into stone and Qi’s birth are commentary, without supplied anatomy. Unit 261 is on scan 30.'),
R('r07-jiang','講山','Mount Jiang','北三十里讲山，多玉柘柏。帝屋椒叶反伤赤实，郭注反伤刺下钩，非反向受伤；御凶为古述，帝字不添神像。','Thirty li north is Mount Jiang, with jade, zhe and bai trees. Diwu has jiao-like leaves, downward-hooked spines and red fruit, with an ancient protective claim.','The hooked-spine detail comes from commentary. The name does not add an emperor or deity figure.'),
R('r07-yingliang','嬰梁','Mount Yingliang','北三十里嬰梁，多苍玉錞于玄石，郭注玉依黑石而生；或解錞于为乐器名是异说，不把两解合成玉钟。265—266续注连读。','Thirty li north is Mount Yingliang, with cang jade associated with dark stone.','The main gloss says jade grows against dark stone; an alternative explains a musical-instrument name. The interpretations are not combined into a jade bell, and the gloss continues across 265–266.'),
R('r07-fuxi','浮戯','Mount Fuxi','东三十里浮戯，亢木樗叶赤实，汜水北注河；东蛇谷多“少辛”，郭注细辛，蛇仅谷名解释不另造独立蛇形。','Thirty li east is Mount Fuxi, with Kang trees, chu-like leaves and red fruit. Si water flows north into the He; Snake valley to the east has shaoxin, glossed as xixin.','The snake-name explanation does not provide an independently described snake. Ancient eating claims are not modern medicinal identifications.'),
R('r07-shaoxing','少陘','Mount Shaoxing','东四十里少陘，𦱌草葵叶赤茎白花蘡薁实，器难水北注役。音刚、古食智述与水名异字分存。270在31页。','Forty li east is Mount Shaoxing, with Gang grass, mallow-like leaves, red stems, white flowers and yingyu-like fruit. Qinan water flows north into Yi water.','Yi is the water named by the service character, not the earlier Yi river. Water-name variants and the ancient intelligence claim remain textual. Unit 270 is on scan 31.'),
R('r07-tai','太山','Mount Tai','东南十里太山，梨草荻叶赤花可已疽；太水出阳东南注没，承水出阴东北注没，古名靖涧注分别存。郭注对东小太山同址存疑，不强定今山。','Ten li southeast is Mount Tai. Li grass has di-like leaves and red flowers, with an ancient sores claim. Tai water rises on the sunny side and flows southeast into Mo; Cheng water rises on the shaded side and flows northeast into Mo.','The source sides and directions stay separate. Guo Pu doubts the contemporary mountain identification and records Jingjian for Cheng water.'),
R('r07-mo','末山','Mount Mo','东二十里末山，上多赤金，末水北注没；水经作沬为郭注异字，山、水、受水体分别存录，不把赤金直接定成现代铜种。','Twenty li east is Mount Mo, with red metal above. Mo water rises here and flows north into the Mo recipient.','Mountain, source water and recipient have separate records. Guo Pu gives a Shui Jing spelling variant; red metal does not establish a modern composition.'),
R('r07-yi','役山','Mount Yi','东二十五里役山，白金铁，役水北注河，与器难水入役关系单列，不并旧伊水。279在32页末。','Twenty-five li east is Mount Yi, with white metal and iron. Yi water rises here and flows north into the He.','This is the service-character Yi water, receiving Qinan separately, not the earlier Yi river. White metal does not fix a modern metal species. Unit 279 is on scan 32.'),
R('r07-min','敏山','Mount Min','东三十五里敏山，葪柏如荆、白花赤实，阳多㻬琈玉。音计及耐寒古述分开，不因柏字强定现代柏树。','Thirty-five li east is Mount Min. Jibai resembles jing, with white flowers and red fruit; tufu jade is abundant on the sunny side.','The pronunciation and ancient endurance-of-cold claim do not identify a modern cypress or a pharmacological effect.'),
R('r07-dagui','大騩','Mount Dagui','东三十里大騩，阴铁美玉青垩。𦵧如蓍而毛、青花白实；尽寿和腹病为古述，或作芺一作巳为异字，不移后世药方。','Thirty li east is Mount Dagui, with iron, fine jade and blue-green e on its shaded side. Lang plants resemble shi, are hairy, and have blue-green flowers and white fruit.','Pronunciation, alternative characters and ancient lifespan and abdominal-illness claims remain separate. The earlier unit-241 mountain is not merged into this one.'),
R('r07-summary','次七总括','Seventh-range summary and rites','苦山列休与至大騩，十九山千一百八十四里。十六神豕身人面、羊羞藻玉瘗，与苦山少室太室三冢人面三首太牢吉玉分别录；三首只明人面未定躯干，图仅头部示意。290冢阅读层恢复，288在33页。','The seventh range from Xiuyu to Dagui reports nineteen mountains and 1,184 li. Sixteen gods have pig bodies and human faces, with sheep offerings and buried multicolored jade. Ku, Shaoshi and Taishi are three distinguished peaks; their gods have human faces and three heads, with grand offerings and auspicious jade.','The other gods remain pig-bodied and human-faced. Three heads do not specify a torso, so the image is a head study only. Ritual animals do not provide deity bodies; the original missing zhong marker stays in captured text.')
]

LINKS=[]
SHARES=[]

def entities(E):
    LINKS.clear();SHARES.clear();out=[];names={r['slug']:r['name'] for r in ROWS};ens={r['slug']:r['en_name'].removeprefix('Mount ') for r in ROWS}
    def add(s,k,key,n,en,q,eq,cn='',note='',**extra):
        out.append(E(s,k,key,n,en,q,cn or '依本段名物、位置与郭注存录，不强定现代种属、成分或坐标。',eq,(eq+' '+note).strip(),**extra));return out[-1]['id']
    def prod(s,key,n,en,q,eq,kind='material',**extra):return add(s,kind,key,n+'（'+names[s]+'）',en+' ('+ens[s]+')',q,eq,**extra)
    def products(s,items):
        for key,n,en,q,k in items:prod(s,key+'-'+s,n,en,q,'The account records '+en+(' on the shaded side.' if '其隂' in q else ' on the sunny side.' if '其陽' in q else ' above.' if '其上' in q else ' below.' if '其下' in q else ' here.'),kind=k)
    def pair(a,b):LINKS.append((a,b))
    def share(id,s,q,eq):SHARES.append((id,s,q,eq))
    def water(s,key,n,en,q,eq,target=None,**extra):
        id=add(s,'water',key,n,en,q,eq,**extra)
        if target:pair(id,target);share(target,s,q,eq)
        return id
    def unknown(s,key,n,en,q,eq,kind='animal',**extra):return add(s,kind,key,n,en,q,eq,'本段无独立可定形貌，或参照/足尾等用词未详；保留占位，不借异篇补成完整物种。','Insufficient independent form evidence; the placeholder is not a depiction.',unknown=True,**extra)
    def form(s,key,n,en,q,eq,cn,note,kind='beast',**extra):return add(s,kind,key,n,en,q,eq,cn,note,**extra)
    def gj(s,q):products(s,[('gold','金','Gold',q,'material'),('jade','玉','Jade',q,'material')])
    he='water-zhongshan-he';yi='water-zhongshan-yi';luo='water-zhongshan-luo';gu='water-zhongshan-gu'
    s='r06-baishi';water(s,'hui-baishi','惠水（白石阳）','Hui water (Baishi sunny side)','惠水出于其陽而南流注于洛','Hui water rises on the sunny side and flows south into the Luo.',luo);prod(s,'water-jade-baishi','水玉','Water jade','其中多水玉','Water jade is abundant in this water account.')
    water(s,'jian-baishi','澗水（白石阴）','Jian water (Baishi shaded side)','澗水出于其隂西北流注于榖水','Jian water rises on the shaded side and flows northwest into Gu water.',gu)
    prod(s,'mi-stone-baishi','麋石','Mi stone','其中多麋石櫨丹','Mi stone and ludan occur in the water account.',commentary='皆未聞',en_commentary='Guo Pu leaves both products unknown.');prod(s,'ludan-baishi','櫨丹','Ludan','其中多麋石櫨丹','Mi stone and ludan occur in the water account.',commentary='皆未聞',en_commentary='Guo Pu leaves both products unknown.')
    s='r06-gu';products(s,[('gu','榖','Gu trees','其上多榖','plant'),('mulberry','桑','Mulberry','其下多桑','plant')]);water(s,'shuang-gu','爽水（榖山）','Shuang water (Gu)','爽水出焉而西北流注于榖水','Shuang water rises here and flows northwest into Gu water.',gu,commentary='世謂之紵麻澗',en_commentary='Guo Pu records Zhuma-jian as a name.');prod(s,'bilu-gu','碧緑','Bi-green material','其中多碧緑','Bi-green material is abundant in the water account.')
    s='r06-mi';products(s,[('jade','玉','Jade','其陽多玉','material'),('iron','鐵','Iron','其隂多鐵','material')]);hao=water(s,'hao-mi','豪水（密山）','Hao water (Mi)','豪水出焉而南流注于洛','Hao water rises here and flows south into the Luo.',luo)
    x=form(s,'xuangui-mi','旋龜（密山）','Xuangui (Mi)','其中多旋龜其狀鳥首而鼈尾其音如判木','Xuangui has a bird head, a softshell-turtle tail and a splitting-wood sound.','鸟首鼈尾据文，普通龟壳四足、短尾细节、配色与姿为解释，不借南山虺尾或添双翼。','Shell styling, ordinary turtle limbs, bird-beak styling and pose are artistic; the Southern snake tail is not transferred.',water=True);pair(hao,x)
    s='r06-changshi';gj(s,'多金玉');add(s,'place','gonggu-changshi','共谷（長石西）','Gong valley (west of Changshi)','其西有谷焉名曰共谷','Gong valley lies to the west.');prod(s,'bamboo-changshi','竹','Bamboo','多竹','Bamboo is abundant in the valley.',kind='plant');water(s,'gong-changshi','共水（長石）','Gong water (Changshi)','共水出焉西南流注于洛','Gong water rises here and flows southwest into the Luo.',luo);prod(s,'ringing-changshi','鳴石','Ringing stone','其中多鳴石','Ringing stone is abundant.',commentary='晉永康元年襄陽郡上鳴石似玉色青撞之聲聞七八里今零𨹧泉𨹧縣永正鄉有鳴石二所其一；狀如皷俗因名為石皷即此𩔖也',en_commentary='The cited ringing-stone examples, color, sound and drum-shaped form continue across 192–193; these do not fix modern mineral identity.')
